      "id": "S12",
      "title": "Epilogue",
      "summary": "Lin Zhixia receives her admission letter. She and Zhou Yu message each other about their majors. She keeps Zhou Yu's pen as a warning.",
      "text": "The day Lin Zhixia's admission letter arrives, her mother wipes the envelope three times before daring to open it. Her phone lights up. A message from Zhou Yu: \"I'm going into teaching. So no one can ever swap a student's score again.\" Lin Zhixia smiles and types back: \"I'm going into law.\" \"Why?\" \"Because the system is still out there. Someone has to watch it.\" She places the pen — Zhou Yu's pen — under the glass on her desk. Beside it, a sticky note: \"This time, every point is mine. Next time, no one takes them.\" But she doesn't throw the pen away. The system didn't disappear. It just changed its shape — waiting for the next person who lends a pen."
